# Phase 5, QUESTION-WORD-LEFT: the word keys at a choice in the model's
# question panel. fx v0.0.16 routes `.word_left` -- what Alt-b decodes to in
# each of its spellings -- with Left to `retreatToPrevious`, the previous page
# of the batch, stopping at the first (`input_question_runtime.zig:190-195`);
# the modified arrows are a composer move there, which a choice leaves alone,
# and so are Alt-f, Ctrl-Right and Right (`:196-199`). Each key is sent from
# page 4, reached the same way every time (Left stops at page 1, then Tab x3),
# so no snap depends on what the key before it did. Last, Alt-b inside a
# draft: the caret's word move, on the same page.
fx: env FX_AUTO_UPGRADE=0
gateway p5-input-question20-turns.json
wait 4
type ask twenty
key Enter
wait 3
key Tab Tab Tab
wait 0.4
snap p4
key M-b
wait 0.4
snap alt-b
key Left Left Left Left
key Tab Tab Tab
wait 0.4
key -H 1b 5b 39 38 3b 33 75
wait 0.4
snap kitty-alt-b
key Left Left Left Left
key Tab Tab Tab
wait 0.4
key -H 1b 5b 32 37 3b 33 3b 39 38 7e
wait 0.4
snap mok-alt-b
key Left Left Left Left
key Tab Tab Tab
wait 0.4
key C-Left
wait 0.4
snap ctrl-left
key Left Left Left Left
key Tab Tab Tab
wait 0.4
key M-Left
wait 0.4
snap alt-left
key Left Left Left Left
key Tab Tab Tab
wait 0.4
key -H 1b 5b 35 37 34 31 37 3b 35 75
wait 0.4
snap kitty-ctrl-left
key Left Left Left Left
key Tab Tab Tab
wait 0.4
key M-f
wait 0.4
snap alt-f
key Left Left Left Left
key Tab Tab Tab
wait 0.4
key C-Right
wait 0.4
snap ctrl-right
key Left Left Left Left
key Tab Tab Tab
wait 0.4
key Right
wait 0.4
snap right
key Left Left Left Left
wait 0.4
key M-b
wait 0.4
snap alt-b-first
key Tab
wait 0.4
type 3
wait 0.4
type ab cd
wait 0.4
key M-b
wait 0.4
type z
wait 0.4
snap draft-alt-b
